    "text": "To solve the expression \\(\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2 - \\cdots}}}}\\), we can denote the entire expression by \\(x\\). This gives us the equation:\n\n\\[ x = \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2 - \\cdots}}}} \\]\n\nSince the expression inside the square root is the same as \\(x\\), we can rewrite the equation as:\n\n\\[ x = \\sqrt{2 - x} \\]\n\nNext, we square both sides of the equation to eliminate the square root:\n\n\\[ x^2 = 2 - x \\]\n\nRearranging the terms gives us a quadratic equation:\n\n\\[ x^2 + x - 2 = 0 \\]\n\nWe can solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\(x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\), where \\(a = 1\\), \\(b = 1\\), and \\(c = -2\\). Plugging in these values, we get:\n\n\\[ x = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot (-2)}}{2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1 + 8}}{2} = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{9}}{2} = \\frac{-1 \\pm 3}{2} \\]\n\nThis gives us two potential solutions:\n\n\\[ x = \\frac{-1 + 3}{2} = \\frac{2}{2} = 1 \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{-1 - 3}{2} = \\frac{-4}{2} = -2 \\]\n\nSince \\(x\\) represents a nested square root expression, it must be a non-negative number. Therefore, we discard the negative solution and keep the positive solution:\n\n\\[ x = 1 \\]\n\nThus, the value of the expression \\(\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2 - \\cdots}}}}\\) is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).",
